        ExerciseCatalogEntry("arnold-press", "Arnold Press", "Front Deltoids", "Dumbbell", "strength_weighted_or_machine", "compound", "Named after the iconic bodybuilder and movie star, the Arnold press adds rotation to a classic shoulder press. It allows the hands to rotate naturally, while also hitting all three heads of the deltoids in one motion. It is usually performed for moderate to high reps, such as 8-12 reps or more, as part of the upper-body or shoulder-focused portion of a workout."),
